# Tablet & Touch UX Invariants

Designed for harsh, fast-paced hotel breakfast environments using mobile and tablet touch devices.

## 1. Input Field Accessibility & Virtual Keyboard
- **NEVER** set `disabled` on primary search or check-in inputs (`#searchInput`, `#tableNumber`, `#actualGuests`) during idle states. Disabling fields prevents the tablet on-screen virtual keyboard from popping up on touch.
- Numeric input fields (`#actualGuests`, guest count fields in modal forms) **MUST** include:
  ```html
  inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" autocomplete="off"
  ```
- Search input fields **MUST** include:
  ```html
  autocomplete="off" autocorrect="off" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false"
  ```

## 2. Touch Delay & CSS Optimizations
- `touch-action: manipulation;` **MUST** be maintained on all interactive elements (`input, select, textarea, button, .search-result, .card, .table-node`) to eliminate the 300ms touch delay on mobile browsers.
- Hardware acceleration (`will-change: transform, opacity;`) and layout containment (`contain: layout style;`) must be preserved for dynamic list items to maintain 60 FPS scrolling on lower-end tablets.

## 3. Focus & Form Navigation
- Upon guest selection or search result enter key, auto-focus on `#tableNumber` input to allow rapid table entry without manual tapping.
- After check-in submission, clear the form inputs and return focus to `#searchInput`.
